@@ -154,15 +154,16 @@ apply only to that side chat. See the [side-chat settings recipe](sessions.md).
 - `list-formatting`: typing `-`, `*`, `1.` or `1)` then Space at the start of a
   line indents it as a list item; the newline gesture continues the list
   (numbers increment) and ends it after an empty item.
-- `palette-new-chat-in-project`: typing in the command palette also lists a
-  **New chat in <project>** row per matching project, which opens the
-  new-session composer with that project's defaults (host, workspace, agent,
-  model, worktree).
 - `focus-hotkey`: Ctrl+Shift+L focuses the in-session message box from anywhere
   in the session view (not on mobile).
 - `new-session-hotkey`: ⌘+Shift+O on macOS or Ctrl+Shift+O on Windows/Linux
   opens and focuses the new-session composer in browsers. Native shells retain
   ⌘/Ctrl+Alt+N. Embedded apps require focus inside the app.
+- `palette-new-chat-in-project`: typing in the ⌘K command palette lists a
+  "New chat in <project>" row per project; every typed word must match, so
+  `project`, `new omni` and `omni` all find it. Choosing a row opens the
+  new-session composer with that project's defaults. The rows are hidden while
+  the query is empty and absent from the sessions-only switcher.
 - `new-session-project-prompt`: when projects exist, the hotkey, the sidebar's
   New session links, and the palette's New chat first ask for a project (or No
   project), then open the composer with its defaults. Settings › General ›
@@ -299,14 +300,12 @@ apply only to that side chat. See the [side-chat settings recipe](sessions.md).
 - Open the host chip, expand **Offline hosts (N)**, then **Show more**. Check the
   same menu on mobile and with a managed sandbox available. Offline rows remain
   disabled; a remembered offline selection still requires an explicit switch.
-- Press ⌘K (macOS) or Ctrl+K (Windows/Linux), or use the sidebar's Search, and
-  type part of a project name, such as `new omni` or `omni`: every typed word
-  must appear in the row label. Choose **New chat in <project>** to land on
-  `/?project=<name>`, the same composer as the project's pencil. The rows stay
-  hidden while the query is empty, and the sessions-only switcher omits them.
 - With the browser app focused, press ⌘+Shift+O (macOS) or
   Ctrl+Shift+O (Windows/Linux) to open and focus a clean new-session
   composer.
+- Press ⌘/Ctrl+K, type part of a project's name (or `project`), and pick
+  **New chat in <project>** to open the new-session composer with that
+  project's host, workspace and agent prefilled.
 - With at least one project, press the hotkey or click New session (also from
   the mobile drawer): a "Start a new session in…" picker opens. Type part of a
   project name and press Enter to land on `/?project=<name>` with its defaults;
@@ -772,10 +771,9 @@ Other connection providers alone do not enable the managed MCP picker.
